    "buying": "Acer is bought from TechZoid by quotation. We do not hold Acer hardware in the online catalogue, so the first step is always a request.\n\n### How an Acer order works\n\n1. Send your requirement through the [enquiry form](/enquiry): model family, quantity, processor class, memory, storage, operating system and warranty.\n2. We obtain pricing and return a written quotation. The price is fixed by that document.\n3. You review it, adjust if needed and issue a purchase order against it.\n4. We deliver and invoice with GST.\n\n### Warranty and onsite service\n\nAcer warranty terms vary with the model and any extension bought with the order. Because school and government sites are often outside metro cities, tell us every delivery location. We state the warranty and any onsite coverage in the quotation, so you know the terms before you commit.\n\n### Bulk and staged delivery\n\nLabs and rollouts seldom need every unit on the same day. If you want deliveries staged by site or by term, put that in the enquiry and we will discuss what can be arranged. Larger quantities are quoted as a whole, so tell us the full count even if you will receive units in phases.\n\n### Tenders and purchase orders\n\nFor education and public-sector buying, send the specification, quantities and delivery clauses. We quote against a written specification and supply a GST invoice that fits into your PO and audit file. If you are running a formal tender, our [IT procurement service](/services/it-procurement) page explains how we handle multi-line orders.\n\n### Software on the same quotation\n\nWindows 11 Pro, [Microsoft 365](/microsoft-365) plans and endpoint backup can be quoted together with the machines. That avoids raising separate purchase orders for hardware and licences.\n\n### What to send\n\n- Model family and quantity for each role.\n- Processor class, memory and storage.\n- Operating system choice.\n- Warranty and onsite needs.\n- Delivery sites and any staging.\n- GST number for the invoice.",
