    "buying": "Acronis is bought through TechZoid by written quotation. There is no catalogue listing or fixed price, because the correct licence set depends on your environment.\n\n### From inventory to quotation\n\n1. Send us the inventory: the number of physical servers, virtual hosts and virtual machines, workstations, and approximate data volume. The [enquiry form](/enquiry) is the easiest route.\n2. Tell us where backups should be stored and the retention you need.\n3. We prepare a written quotation naming the editions, the counts and the term. That quotation fixes the price.\n4. You raise a purchase order and we invoice with GST at 18%.\n\n### Activation and onboarding\n\nTechZoid helps with activation and with assigning licences to the right machines. Deployment design, storage sizing and recovery testing are separate work; our [backup and disaster recovery service](/services/backup-disaster-recovery) is where that is handled.\n\n### Subscription terms and renewals\n\nAcronis licences are commonly sold as subscriptions, and some products offer other models. Say in your enquiry which term you prefer and whether you want renewal reminders. The quotation will state the term and what it covers, so you can budget for renewal.\n\n### Tenders and purchase orders\n\nIf you are responding to a tender or buying against a purchase order, share the specification clauses on backup, retention and recovery. We quote against what is written, and the GST invoice can go into your records.\n\n### Pairing with other purchases\n\nBackup is often bought alongside new servers, Microsoft licences or Microsoft 365. Because TechZoid supplies those too, they can sit on one quotation. For hosted mail and files, check how [Microsoft 365](/microsoft-365) data is protected before deciding what Acronis should cover.\n\n### What to send us\n\n- Count of servers, virtual machines and workstations.\n- Total data size and growth expectation.\n- Storage location and retention needs.\n- Preferred term and edition.\n- GST number and delivery contact for licence details.",
