    "intro": "Dell is the name most Indian IT heads reach for first when a server room needs new hardware. Its enterprise range is built around PowerEdge servers in rack and tower form, PowerStore for shared storage, and Precision workstations for design and engineering. Between them they cover the file server in a branch office, the virtualisation cluster in a head office and the workstation under an engineer's desk.\n\nThe TechZoid catalogue carries real Dell listings: eight PowerEdge rack models, three PowerEdge tower models, PowerStore storage and the Precision workstation. We do not list Dell laptops, desktops or monitors, so this page is about data-centre and workstation hardware only. None of it carries a price on the website. A server is quoted to configuration and quantity, because processors, memory, drive bays, network cards, power supplies and support term all change the figure, and a single displayed number would only mislead.\n\nIn practice the catalogue pages work as a shortlist. Pick the models that fit, note what you want changed, and send it to us. We come back with a written quotation, and that document fixes the price. Every order carries a GST invoice, which GST-registered buyers can usually claim as input credit.\n\nTechZoid is a Dell reseller, and that is all we claim. We quote and supply, we help you put the specification together, and we can include the operating system, virtualisation licensing, database licences and backup on the same quotation, so the purchase order is raised once. If you are comparing Dell against another server maker for the same project, the [HP](/brands/hp) and [HPE](/brands/hpe) hubs and our [IT procurement service](/services/it-procurement) page cover the alternatives and how multi-line purchases are handled.",
