    "choose": "Start with where the server will live and what it will run, then use the catalogue pages to confirm the model.\n\nChoose a tower when the server sits in an ordinary office or branch with no rack and a handful of users depending on it. Choose a rack server when you already have a rack, expect to add more servers, or are consolidating several workloads onto virtualisation hosts. The model number generally rises with capability, so the smaller models suit file, print and light application duties, while the larger ones suit heavier virtualisation and database work. Within a family, newer models are usually the better long-term buy if the project must last several years, though availability changes, so ask us what can be quoted today.\n\nWhen you write to us, give the following so every quotation is comparable:\n\n- **Workload.** File server, virtualisation host, database, backup target or application server.\n- **Users and growth.** Roughly how many people depend on it now and in three years.\n- **Capacity.** Storage you need, and whether it should be internal drives or shared storage such as PowerStore.\n- **Resilience.** Whether you need redundant power, drive protection or a second server for failover.\n- **Support term.** The warranty or ProSupport level you want, and the locations that need onsite cover.\n\nIf the machine is a workstation, name the application and the publisher's recommended graphics and memory, and we will quote to match.",
    "buying": "Dell hardware on TechZoid is quoted, never priced on the page. The listings tell you what the server is; the quotation tells you what it costs for your configuration and quantity.\n\n### From catalogue page to quotation\n\n1. Open the listings you are considering, for instance the [PowerEdge R760](/products/dell-poweredge-r760) or the [PowerEdge T360](/products/dell-poweredge-t360).\n2. Send us the models, quantities and any changes to memory, drives, network or support term through the [enquiry form](/enquiry).\n3. We reply with a written quotation. That is the price; nothing on the website is.\n4. You raise a purchase order against the quotation and we invoice with GST.\n\n### Warranty and ProSupport\n\nServers normally come with a manufacturer warranty, and Dell offers higher service levels, including its ProSupport range, as upgrades. The exact term, response commitment and onsite coverage depend on the model, the level chosen at the time of order and the location. Tell us the cities where the hardware will sit, and we will state the support terms in the quotation so they are on record before you commit.\n\n### Operating system, virtualisation and database on one quotation\n\nA server is rarely useful until it is licensed. TechZoid supplies Microsoft licensing, so you can ask for [Windows Server 2025 Standard](/products/windows-server-2025-standard) for physical or lightly virtualised hosts, [Windows Server 2025 Datacenter](/products/windows-server-2025-datacenter) for heavily virtualised hosts, [user CALs](/products/windows-server-cal-user) for the people who connect, and [SQL Server 2022 Standard](/products/sql-server-2022-standard) where a database is needed. Licensing rules depend on core counts, so give us the processor configuration and we will size the licences to the hardware.\n\n### Backup and recovery\n\nA new server needs a recovery plan from day one. Add [backup software](/backup-software) to the same quotation, or read about our [backup and disaster recovery service](/services/backup-disaster-recovery) if you want help designing it.\n\n### Tenders and purchase orders\n\nFor government, university and public-sector tenders, send the specification and the delivery and warranty clauses. We quote against a written specification and issue a GST invoice, so the quotation and invoice can go into your PO file. Staged delivery across locations can be discussed and recorded in the quotation.\n\n### Information that speeds up the quote\n\n- Models from the catalogue, with quantities.\n- Workload, memory, drive capacity and network needs.\n- Operating system, virtualisation and database licences required.\n- Support term and onsite requirements.\n- Delivery locations, and your GST number for the invoice.",
